<.page_header>
  <:eyebrow>CNA Console</:eyebrow>
  <:title>Link this provider?</:title>
  <:subtitle>You signed in with a provider while already holding another account.</:subtitle>
</.page_header>

<.page_container class="space-y-4">
  <div class="rounded-box border border-base-300 p-4 space-y-3">
    <p>
      You started this from <span class="font-semibold">{@linking_from.display_name}</span>
      and have just signed in as <span class="font-semibold">{@signed_in.display_name}</span>.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
      Linking hands this provider to <span class="font-medium">{@linking_from.display_name}</span>, along with
      anything the other account is currently working on — case assignments, API
      tokens, open proposals. What it has already written stays credited to it,
      and it will no longer be a way to sign in.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 pt-1">
      <.form for={%{}} action={~p"/settings/account/link/confirm"} method="post">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-eef">Link to {@linking_from.display_name}</button>
      </.form>
      <.form for={%{}} action={~p"/settings/account/link/decline"} method="post">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost">Keep separate accounts</button>
      </.form>
    </div>

    <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60">
      Keeping them separate leaves you signed in as <span class="font-medium">{@signed_in.display_name}</span>; nothing is
      merged, and you can link them later from the account page.
    </p>
  </div>
</.page_container>
